# Working notes and reference material — kept locally, not published.
#
# ...except the research record. ROADMAP.md and the *_AB.md pre-registrations
# ARE the project's evidence: each one states a bar before a run and the result
# after it, and a result whose configuration is lost is not a result. They were
# tracked at the repo root; moving them under docs/ must not quietly untrack
# them, which a bare `docs/` would do — the directory ignore is why §3 already
# records a "Session 2 audit" document nobody can find.
#
# Everything else here (STATE_OF_PLAY.md, the playbook PDF, handover notes)
# stays local exactly as before.
#
# The exceptions must be repeated per directory. A pattern only matches one
# path segment, and git does not descend into an ignored directory at all — so
# `!docs/*_AB.md` stopped matching the moment those files moved into
# docs/evidence/, and five tracked files silently became deletions.
docs/*
!docs/ROADMAP.md
!docs/README.md
!docs/STATE_OF_MERIDIAN_*.md

# The evidence: pre-registrations, and the index that says how each one landed.
!docs/evidence/
docs/evidence/*
!docs/evidence/*_AB.md
!docs/evidence/PHASE_B_IC.md
!docs/evidence/PHASE_C_COMBINE.md
!docs/evidence/PHASE_D_NONLINEAR.md
!docs/evidence/STAGE0_MAKER_FILL.md
!docs/evidence/CROSS_VENUE_PREREG.md
!docs/evidence/README.md

# The current plan. Everything else under active/ is a working note.
# docs/active/ is gone as of 1 Sept 2026 — both documents in it were finished
# and moved to archive/. RESEARCH_PLAN was tracked and public, so the exception
# follows it to its new path rather than silently untracking it.
!docs/archive/
docs/archive/*
!docs/archive/RESEARCH_PLAN_*.md

# Python bytecode from the research venv.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Research venv (numpy/pandas/scikit-learn). Pinned in research/requirements.txt.
.venv-research/
